From c17ffb2516fec3126801c03d1ab3bfba64965ff4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: robertlipe <8724975+robertlipe@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 09:10:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Refactor: Modernize C++ core components with C++20 features

* Replace `PI`, `TWO_PI`, and `M_PI` math macros with `<numbers>` constants
* Convert prominent manual C-style arrays (`rules`, `digits`, `screen`, `ReelPos`) to `std::array` with CTAD where applicable
* Replace unsafe `memset` and `memcpy` calls in core engine networking buffers with `<algorithm>` functions (`std::copy`, `std::fill`) or brace-enclosed zero-initialization (`{}`)
* Safely wrap raw pointer memory allocations and task lifecycle management in `taskmgr.cpp` and `remotecontrol.cpp` into `std::unique_ptr` and `std::make_shared_psram` to properly transfer ownership to tasks and eliminate memory leaks
* Convert manual looping sequences in `debug_cli.cpp` and `remotecontrol.cpp` to canonical classic `<algorithm>` standards (`std::find_if`, `std::vector::insert`) without using `<ranges>` to preserve ESP32 flash constraints.
---
